components.key_interactions:
Called only by adminCommentRemove. Once removed_at is set, visibleSQL hides the row everywhere with no further code:
- treeSQL blanks it;
- arrange keeps it as a placeholder or drops it;
- Post refuses replies under it;
- Visible stops counting it.

components.responsibility:
**report.html:** add `<p class="comment-count">{{.CommentCount}} {{if eq .CommentCount 1}}comment{{else}}comments{{end}}</p>` directly after `<p class="likes">…</p>` inside section#votes. This is spike placement F1, number first, in its own block.

**comments.html:** in the 'comment' template's non-placeholder branch, after the Reply details, add `{{if .CanRemove}}<details class="remove"><summary>Remove</summary><form method="post" action="/admin/comments/{{.ID}}/remove"><button type="submit">Remove for everyone</button></form></details>{{end}}`. The control:
- carries no hidden field, because reader pages carry no page-dependent field (#950);
- has no digit in any text, aria-label or alt;
- does not use the word 'comment' in its labels, because the finish readers fold aria-label and alt into the pieces they count.

Any CSS added to site.css for .remove or .comment-count avoids pure #ff0000 or #00ff00 ±8 (#941).

adminReport (admin.go) reads nodes through a.tree(ctx, rep.ID) after OwnerInbox. An error gives 500, never an empty list. adminData gains Moderation []modItem = moderationList(nodes, a.cfg.OwnerGitHubID). Drafts and unpublished reports are listed, because treeSQL filters only on report_id.

The template gains `<section class="moderation" id="comments"><h2>Comments</h2>` directly after the feedback inbox. Each item is an `<article class="mod">` holding:
- `<header class="byline">` with avatar, login, Author badge and time in the admin format;
- `<p class="reply-to">` reading 'top level', 'in reply to @login' or 'in reply to a removed comment', in its own block so no date digit sits beside 'comment';
- `<p class="body">`;
- the same remove details, whose form also carries `<input type="hidden" name="from" value="admin">`.

When nothing is visible it shows `<p>Nothing visible on this report.</p>`. The section has no count line, no element whose id is comment-<n> or feedback-<n>, and no number beside a dislike label. Removed text is shown to nobody, the owner included.

